  "review": "The generic rhsWith definition matches both existing RHS definitions in all six node cases. Its degree proof uses the original case argument with a wire-degree hypothesis, and both existing rhs_degree statements specialize it. Existing definitions, public theorem statements and imports are unchanged. All recorded statuses, logs and output object hashes were checked; 12 current source hashes and imports match the graph, and the four borrowed object/source hashes match successful earlier receipts. Scoped logs contain no warnings.",
  "limitations": [
    "The new-helper and inferred-instance probe exit statuses were observed by the author but not saved as standalone machine-readable status records; their source and output logs are retained.",
    "Four prerequisite objects were borrowed from authenticated earlier rebuilds and two were freshly rebuilt; other project and external dependencies remain precompiled, so this is not a full dependency-closure build.",
    "The three new/promoted helpers use the standard three axioms except rhsWith, which is axiom-free.",
    "Target object sizes changed from 508608 to 542664 and from 448936 to 426952 bytes; timing observations were concurrent and do not establish a speedup.",
    "Objects and overlay symlinks are excluded; recorded paths refer to the original local validation environment."
